	"name": "Waste Not",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/commodities/tech/pipe-metal.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Living in the wasteland means nothing goes to waste. You gain proficiency with Improvised Weapons, and if you have access to a power source or ammunition and scrap materials you can cobble together improvised blaster weapons. Any improvised blaster weapon you create has a range of 30/60ft and deals 1d6 + Dexterity modifier fire, piercing, or radiant damage, chosen when you piece the weapon together. It can fire a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus before it is rendered useless. You can create one such weapon per short or long rest, but may not create another until the first is depleted or destroyed.</p>",
